# PLATFORM

Platform architecture repository entrypoint. Owns the durable production and
operational integration baseline for one or more governed `platform_id` values.

## Read First

1. This file - Platform context and navigation

## Parent

- [ENTERPRISE](<enterprise-repo-url>/blob/main/ENTERPRISE.md)

If enterprise level is absent in your organization, replace with `Not applicable`.

## Critical File Contract

- Keep required section headings from this template.
- Keep this file concise: identity, routing semantics, and links.
- Put mutable runtime state and telemetry in runtime-owned systems, not here.
- If a required section has no content, keep it and write `Not applicable`.

## Knowledge Store Layout

```text
PLATFORM.md                                        <- you are here
AGENTS.md                                          <- repo-specific instructions
platform-implementations.yml                       <- implementation routing
architecture/
`-- platforms/
    `-- <platform_id>/
        |-- platform-design.yml                    <- durable platform baseline
        |-- connection-catalog.yml                 <- connection_id definitions
        |-- operational-guardrails.yml             <- resilience/security/SLOs
        `-- runbooks/                               <- support navigation
inputs/
`-- workstreams/
    `-- <WORKSTREAM_ID>/
        |-- WORKSTREAM.md                          <- workstream navigation
        `-- platform-change-handoff.yml            <- optional requested change
```

## Canonical Artifacts

- `platform-implementations.yml` (`implementation_id` routing)
- `architecture/platforms/<platform_id>/platform-design.yml`
- `architecture/platforms/<platform_id>/connection-catalog.yml`
- operational guardrails and runbook references owned by Platform/SRE

## Routing

`implementation_id` -> `platform-implementations.yml` -> `repo.url` +
`repo.paths` + optional `repo.entrypoint` + optional `repo.git_ref`

## Platform Identity

The ownership identity is `platform_id`. Inbound `workstream_id` values are
Initiative demand units attached to this durable Platform authority; they do
not create independent Platform runtimes. `platform_repo_url` in the Enterprise
registry is authoritative when the registry is available.

## Integration Ownership

- The providing Domain or component owns the stable semantic contract
  (`interface_id`).
- Platform owns the deployed and operated realization (`connection_id`),
  including brokers, gateways, endpoints, queues/topics, network paths,
  security, capacity, resilience, observability, and support procedures.
- Integration is covered by Platform; it is not a separate architecture level.

## Upstream Inputs

- Resolve Initiative demand through `platform-workstreams.yml`.
- Open the Workstream-specific `WORKSTREAM.md` at `workstream_git_ref`.
- Verify any `change_handoff_ref` against exact Git bytes before routing or
  dispatch.

## Policy

- Treat `platform_id`, `connection_id`, `workstream_id`, and implementation
  selectors as authoritative identities.
- Fail closed on missing, ambiguous, inactive, or unverified routing inputs.
- Keep runtime progress and operability evidence outside routing catalogs.
